zoe (docs): Hey team — I'm assembling a compact "Error playbook" for 429s, request timeouts, and context-limit fallout. Want: tiny py/js snippets, a customer checklist, and a short migration note about trim helpers. Can someone take a pass?

ryan (eng-runtime): Heads-up: 429s typically mean serving queue/concurrency hit. Responses MAY include `Retry-After` (secs). Recommend: honor `Retry-After` if present; otherwise exponential backoff + full jitter. After ~3 retries, suggest failing over to a lighter model or surfacing a clear client error. For timeouts, call out KV-cache cold starts and prefilling.

anya (devex): I can add snippets. Quick JS example using AbortController + retry/backoff:```js
async function requestWithRetries(url, opts = {}, maxRetries = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i <= maxRetries; i++) {
    const ctrl = new AbortController();
    const timeout = setTimeout(() => ctrl.abort(), opts.timeout || 60000);
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, { ...opts, signal: ctrl.signal });
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      if (res.status === 429) {
        const ra = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
        const wait = ra ? Number(ra) : Math.min(Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random(), 30);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error('http error');
      return await res.json();
    } catch (err) {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      if (err.name === 'AbortError' && i < maxRetries) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, (Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random()) * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
}
```

anya (devex): Python example (requests + jitter):```python
import time, random
import requests

def post_with_backoff(url, payload, max_retries=3, timeout=60):
    for attempt in range(max_retries + 1):
        r = requests.post(url, json=payload, timeout=timeout)
        if r.status_code == 429:
            ra = r.headers.get('Retry-After')
            wait = int(ra) if ra and ra.isdigit() else min((2 ** attempt) + random.random(), 30)
            time.sleep(wait)
            continue
        r.raise_for_status()
        return r.json()
    raise RuntimeError('retries exhausted')
```

sam (support): Add a short customer checklist please: 1) If you see 429s after deploy, reduce `max_response_tokens` and trim history; 2) enable client-side concurrency limits; 3) try fallback models (e.g., `redwood-lite`) or quantized variants; 4) collect request ids/timestamps and open a ticket. Note: Dedicated pools can be increased for sustained throughput.

zoe (docs): Migration note: older SDKs (pre-v1.3) used `trim_history()` which estimated by message count. Newer SDKs expose `trim_by_tokens()` (token-accurate). Suggest adding code pointer and mark under "Migration notes".

ryan (eng-runtime): Also call out KV-cache warmup: after scaling new workers, first requests may hit higher latency or timeouts. Recommend a short warmup pass (prefetch common prefixes) or retry-once with jitter. Mention streaming can be truncated mid-token when forced truncation occurs.

